IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sscba-types`
IMPORT `sscba-rules`
IMPORT `sscba-goal`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (UK) — the encoder's
-- tests. Expected values are worked by hand from the Act.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Goal 1 — Class 1 contributions`

-- £1,000 in a week; PT £242, UEL £967, ST £96.
GIVEN pay IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Week of earnings`
`a week paid` pay MEANS `Week of earnings` OF pay, 242, 967, 96, 15

#ASSERT `the primary Class 1 contribution on` (`a week paid` 1000) EQUALS 58.66
#ASSERT `the secondary Class 1 contribution on` (`a week paid` 1000) EQUALS 135.6
#ASSERT `the primary Class 1 contribution on` (`a week paid` 500) EQUALS 20.64
#ASSERT `the primary Class 1 contribution on` (`a week paid` 200) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the secondary Class 1 contribution on` (`a week paid` 90) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the primary Class 1 contribution on` (`a week paid` 967) EQUALS 58
-- An age-related 0% secondary rate.
#ASSERT `the secondary Class 1 contribution on` (`Week of earnings` OF 1000, 242, 967, 96, 0) EQUALS 0

§§ `Goal 2 — statutory sick pay`

GIVEN nwe IS A NUMBER, qd IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Sick pay facts`
`sick, earning` nwe `, qualifying days` qd MEANS `Sick pay facts` OF nwe, qd, NOTHING, Date 1 3 2026

#ASSERT `the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` (`sick, earning` 200 `, qualifying days` 5) EQUALS 123.25
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` (`sick, earning` 100 `, qualifying days` 5) EQUALS 80
#ASSERT `the statutory sick pay for a day for` (`sick, earning` 100 `, qualifying days` 5) EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `the statutory sick pay for a day for` (`sick, earning` 200 `, qualifying days` 7) EQUALS 123.25 DIVIDED BY 7
#ASSERT `the entitlement limit for` (`sick, earning` 200 `, qualifying days` 5) EQUALS 3451
-- s 152(3): ended 1 March, next began 27 April: 56 days between — linked;
-- 28 April: 57 — not.
#ASSERT `the periods of incapacity link for` (`Sick pay facts` OF 100, 5, JUST (Date 1 3 2026), Date 27 4 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`the periods of incapacity link for` (`Sick pay facts` OF 100, 5, JUST (Date 1 3 2026), Date 28 4 2026))

§§ `Goal 3 — statutory maternity pay`

-- Expected 15 July 2026 (a Wednesday): the expected week begins Sunday 12
-- July. The 15th week before begins 29 March; the 11th, 26 April. 26 weeks
-- ending with the 15th week begin 5 October 2025.
GIVEN began IS A DATE, nwe IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Maternity facts`
`expecting 15 July 2026, employed from` began `, earning` nwe `, on` d MEANS
    `Maternity facts` OF Date 15 7 2026, began, TRUE, nwe, 129, d, FALSE, 194.32

#ASSERT `the expected week of confinement begins for` (`expecting 15 July 2026, employed from` (Date 1 1 2020) `, earning` 500 `, on` (Date 1 5 2026)) EQUALS Date 12 7 2026
#ASSERT `the earliest start of the maternity pay period for` (`expecting 15 July 2026, employed from` (Date 1 1 2020) `, earning` 500 `, on` (Date 1 5 2026)) EQUALS Date 26 4 2026
#ASSERT `is entitled to statutory maternity pay` (`expecting 15 July 2026, employed from` (Date 5 10 2025) `, earning` 500 `, on` (Date 26 4 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled to statutory maternity pay` (`expecting 15 July 2026, employed from` (Date 6 10 2025) `, earning` 500 `, on` (Date 26 4 2026)))
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled to statutory maternity pay` (`expecting 15 July 2026, employed from` (Date 5 10 2025) `, earning` 500 `, on` (Date 25 4 2026)))
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled to statutory maternity pay` (`expecting 15 July 2026, employed from` (Date 5 10 2025) `, earning` 128 `, on` (Date 26 4 2026)))
-- An expected date on a Sunday starts its own week.
#ASSERT `the expected week of confinement begins for` (`Maternity facts` OF Date 12 7 2026, Date 1 1 2020, TRUE, 500, 129, Date 1 5 2026, FALSE, 194.32) EQUALS Date 12 7 2026
-- Rates: 90% of £500 = £450; later weeks the lower of £450 and £194.32.
#ASSERT `the first 6 weeks' rate for` (`expecting 15 July 2026, employed from` (Date 1 1 2020) `, earning` 500 `, on` (Date 1 5 2026)) EQUALS 450
#ASSERT `the later weeks' rate for` (`expecting 15 July 2026, employed from` (Date 1 1 2020) `, earning` 500 `, on` (Date 1 5 2026)) EQUALS 194.32
#ASSERT `the later weeks' rate for` (`expecting 15 July 2026, employed from` (Date 1 1 2020) `, earning` 200 `, on` (Date 1 5 2026)) EQUALS 180

§§ `The top-level goal`

pos MEANS `the employee position for` (`Employee case` OF JUST (`a week paid` 1000), NOTHING, JUST (`expecting 15 July 2026, employed from` (Date 1 1 2020) `, earning` 500 `, on` (Date 1 5 2026)))
#ASSERT pos's `primary Class 1 contribution` EQUALS JUST 58.66
#ASSERT pos's `entitled to statutory maternity pay` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT pos's `maternity pay for the first 6 weeks` EQUALS JUST 450
#ASSERT pos's `weekly statutory sick pay` EQUALS NOTHING
